+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-spec-001"></a>
+
+The same directory is also published the other way round. A page lists every specialty the clinic knows, each under its stored name, with the veterinarians holding it `[REQ-SPEC-001]`. Each holder is named in full: first name, then last name. The whole list appears at once rather than a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is named nowhere, because the page lists specialties rather than the roster. The page is reached by its own address alone, and nothing in the interface links to it (stated 2026-08-14).
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given the specialties the clinic knows, when the specialty directory is opened, then every one of them is listed under its stored name.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a specialty held by at least one veterinarian, when the directory is opened, then each holder is named by first name followed by last name.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is named nowhere on it.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given any number of specialties, when the directory is opened, then all of them appear on the one page, with no paging control.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given every page of the interface, when each is rendered, then none of them links to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A veterinarian holding more than one specialty is named under each of them.
+2. A specialty no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian named under it.
+3. A clinic with no specialty recorded shows the page with nothing listed rather than failing.
+4. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts) · **ADR:** [ADR: Specialty Directory Derived in Memory from the Cached Veterinarian List](adr/2026-08-14-specialty-directory-derived-in-memory.md)
+
